---
description: QA Garage operating rules
alwaysApply: true
---

This repository is a portable AI-native QA Garage. It wraps a library of vendored QA skills in `.agents/skills/` with a thin harness layer that keeps the human in control.

Before QA-related work, read:

- `core/ai/qa-principles.md`
- `core/ai/qa-garage-operating-model.md`
- `core/ai/qa-project-context-model.md`
- `core/ai/discovery-workflow.md`
- `core/ai/knowledge-maintenance.md`
- `core/ai/test-design-principles.md`
- `core/ai/human-decides-loop.md`
- `core/ai/daily-qa-loop.md`
- `core/ai/task-tracking-workflow.md`
- `core/ai/qa-cadence.md`
- `core/ai/scope-proposal-workflow.md`

Then use the vendored skills in `.agents/skills/` for QA craft. The harness routes via `core/ai/qa-garage-operating-model.md` and thin wrappers in `core/skills/`.

Each target project is its own QA root at `projects/<project>/`. Read `.agents/qa-project-context.md` and `reference/` first. Targets are black-box: source from docs and exploration.

Use deterministic automation as the source of truth. Playwright output, traces, reports, `qa-project-context.md`, `reference/`, and `tasks/qa-tasks.md` outrank unsourced AI judgment.

End every session with harness `knowledge-curator` (see `knowledge-maintenance.md`).

AI may explore, reproduce bugs, draft tests, propose jobs, draft scope proposals, classify failures, write reports, and recommend improvements.

AI must not automatically:

- Change assertions.
- Delete or skip tests.
- Update visual baselines.
- Redefine expected behavior.
- Promote observed or inferred knowledge to confirmed.
- Mark human review as approved without approval.
- Send client proposals without QA Lead approval.
- Hide or relabel failures to make a run look green.

## Gates

- **Discovery gate (soft):** Phase 0 and reference updates are not blocked by access questions.
- **Execution gate:** Do not begin execution-gated work while blocking items exist in `open-items.md` unless `decisions.md` overrides. Run `QA_PROJECT=<project> npm run qa:review -- --gate`.

End every working turn that produced open items with an ACTION REQUIRED summary. Humans answer via `questions.md` and `decisions.md` — see `human-decides-loop.md`.
